 "notes": [
  "Requested niphal sense \"wink\" and hiphil senses \"make a twinkling (of an eye); harden\" have zero verbal attestation. The lexicon's meaning field mentions \"wink (from the motion of the eye-lids)\" only as an etymological aside tied to the cognate noun רֶגַע (\"a wink of the eyes, i.e. a very short space of time\", H7281) -- its own usage list for the verb (break, divide, find ease, be a moment, (cause/give/make to) rest, make suddenly) has no \"wink\" or \"harden\" gloss, and none of the actual niphal/hiphil citations support them. Niphal's sole attestation (Jer.47.6, imperative to a sword) is \"be still\"; excluded \"wink\". Hiphil's 8 attestations split between \"give rest\" (Jer.31.2, Isa.34.14, Deut.28.65, Isa.51.4) and an idiomatic \"in/for a moment, suddenly\" (Jer.49.19, Jer.50.44, Prov.12.19); excluded \"make a twinkling of an eye\" and \"harden\"."
 ],
